A utility process on the Linux family without Linux's kernel still starts
tracing after the sandbox it does not have.

Patch 0047 gated the whole Linux arm of UtilityMain on HAS_LINUX_KERNEL,
which is right for what most of it is - seccomp-bpf, the pre-sandbox hooks,
the zygote - and wrong for the last two things in it. ContentMainRunnerImpl
defers startup tracing to "after sandbox initialisation" for every non-GPU
child on this family (needs_startup_tracing_after_sandbox_init), and the
renderer's arm kept its InitTracingPostFeatureList; the utility's went with
the sandbox. So the network service and the storage service each registered
their first perfetto data source - memory_instrumentation::ClientProcessImpl,
inside ChildThreadImpl::Init, before anything else runs - against the fake
muxer, which is PERFETTO_FATAL: a ud2, SIGILL, and a child that dies a second
after it starts, with its last words on a descriptor that until M171 went
nowhere. [m167] counted it as "a storage service that died" and did not ask
why.

This is M164's sentence one more time - a gate on a definition takes a
caller with it - and the shape of the fix is the same: a second arm of the
same #if for the Linux family as a whole, carrying only the half that is
not about the sandbox.

diff --git a/content/utility/utility_main.cc b/content/utility/utility_main.cc
index 0596792..522cd9d 100644
--- a/content/utility/utility_main.cc
+++ b/content/utility/utility_main.cc
@@ -431,6 +431,30 @@ int UtilityMain(MainFunctionParams parameters) {
     base::HangWatcher::GetInstance()->Start();
   }
 
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
+  // The Linux family without Linux's kernel: no seccomp sandbox to enter,
+  // but the two things above that are not about the sandbox still have to
+  // happen, because ContentMainRunnerImpl deferred them here for every
+  // non-GPU child on this family. A utility process that skips the tracing
+  // initialisation registers its first data source against the fake muxer,
+  // which is fatal - ChildThreadImpl::Init does it through
+  // memory_instrumentation::ClientProcessImpl before anything else runs.
+  if (parameters.needs_startup_tracing_after_sandbox_init) {
+    tracing::InitTracingPostFeatureList(/*enable_consumer=*/false,
+                                        /*will_trace_thread_restart=*/false);
+  }
+
+  if (base::HangWatcher::IsEnabled() &&
+      !base::HangWatcher::GetInstance()->IsStarted()) {
+    DCHECK(parameters.hang_watcher_not_started_time.has_value());
+    base::TimeDelta uncovered_hang_watcher_time =
+        base::TimeTicks::Now() -
+        parameters.hang_watcher_not_started_time.value();
+    base::UmaHistogramTimes("HangWatcher.UtilityProcess.UncoveredStartupTime",
+                            uncovered_hang_watcher_time);
+    base::HangWatcher::GetInstance()->Start();
+  }
+
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
   std::optional<base::win::ScopedCOMInitializer> scoped_com_initializer;
   if (message_pump_type == base::MessagePumpType::UI) {
